In traditional \TeX{} workflows, marking up abbreviations is both
tedious and fragile: once an abbreviation is introduced, authors
must both revisit earlier text and remember to apply the same markup
throughout the remainder of the document. In practice, this often
leads to inconsistencies or omitted abbreviation markup.

This article presents new support for abbreviations in the Markdown
package for \TeX, shifting abbreviation handling from a procedural
to a more declarative model. Editors can predefine standard
abbreviations, while authors mark up individual occurrences as
needed; the package then ensures that these abbreviations, whether
introduced by editors or authors, are formatted consistently
throughout the document.
